[0.007751, "o", "\u001b[1;36m$ claude\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;33m> PROMPT:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.009811, "o", "  Read CLAUDE.md. Final QA session.\r\n  \r\n  1. Run npm run validate, npm run test, npm run build. Fix any failures.\r\n  2. Review App.jsx and components for bugs: NaN handling when grade input is empty or out of range, division by zero, filter combinations that contradict (max total cost lower than cheapest tuition), letter-grade edge cases. Fix what you find and extend scripts/test-match.mjs with regressions.\r\n  3. Add a README.md: what the app is, screenshot placeholder, how matching works (the formula), how to run, how to deploy to Vercel.\r\n  4. Add vercel.json if needed for a Vite SPA, and a .gitignore.\r\n  5. Leave the repo clean: git init, initial commit with a conventional message.\r\n"]
[0.009992, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m--- Claude Code session start ---\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[442.352606, "o", "All five QA tasks are done:\r\n\r\n1. **`validate`/`test`/`build`** all passed cleanly with no fixes needed.\r\n2. **Bug review** — found and fixed one real defensive gap: `ProfileForm` only checked for an empty grade string, then called `onSubmit` with raw `grade`/`scale`, and `App.jsx` called `toGPA` uncaught — any value that made `toGPA` throw (blank/partial-number strings, an unrecognized letter grade) would crash the whole app with no error boundary. I moved the `toGPA` conversion + try/catch into `ProfileForm`, so it now surfaces a friendly inline error instead of white-screening, and `App.jsx` only ever receives an already-valid `{ gpa, interests }`. Everything else checked out already: `match.js` guards interest-fit division by zero, out-of-range numeric grades clamp instead of erroring, and contradictory cost filters (`maxTotalCost` below available tuition) already degrade gracefully to a \"no results / relax filters\" empty state rather than crashing. I extracted the inline filter/sort logic from `App.jsx` into `src/lib/filters.js` so it's unit-testable, and extended `scripts/test-match.mjs` from 8 to 19 assertions covering NaN/blank/partial-number inputs, letter-grade case/whitespace/near-miss edge cases, label boundary conditions, zero-interest-overlap scoring, and contradictory-filter/empty-sort regressions.\r\n3. **README.md** added — what the app is, a screenshot placeholder note, the match-score formula and label thresholds, run instructions, and Vercel deploy steps.\r\n4. **`vercel.json`** added (SPA rewrite to `index.html`) and **`.gitignore`** expanded (env files, editor dirs, `.vercel`, etc.), while keeping the existing `prompts/`, `recordings/`, `transcripts/` content tracked since it looked like intentional project material rather than build output.\r\n5. **Git initialized**, branch renamed to `main`, secrets-scanned before staging, and committed everything (except `node_modules`/`dist`) in one conventional-style initial commit.\r\n"]
[442.617513, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m--- session complete (exit 0) ---\u001b[0m\r\n"]
